# THE REASON THIS FILE EXISTS.
#
# This repository is public, and the README's first promise is that no business
# data is in it: no data snapshot, no exported report, no figure of any kind
# baked into the markup. Every number the console shows is fetched at view time
# under the reader's own login, and row-level security decides what they see.
#
# Rendering the console offline — for a layout check or a screenshot — needs
# real rows, and the natural way to get them is to dump a series into a file
# beside index.html. Such a file is exactly the data snapshot the README says is
# not here: __harness.js at the time of writing held ~900 days of signed and
# invoiced dollars per brand. It was never committed, but nothing stopped it
# either, and one `git add -A` from any session would have published it.
#
# Keep render harnesses OUT of the working tree where possible (a scratch
# directory outside the repo is better). When one must live here, it matches a
# pattern below and stays untracked.
__harness.js
*-harness.html
*-harness.js
harness-data.*
console-data.json
series.txt
*.local.json

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
